dsnoek@terapin.com (Daniel Snoek) writes:

>What's the newest version of Hack?  I remember playing it a few years back, is
>it the same ascii game with text graphics?

It's called NetHack++ and yes, it's still the same ASCII game. Although there
exists a Hack-Lite for the CBM Amiga. I don't like the graphics version, the
monsters are too small and sometimes it's hard to see what they are. The
SM-DOS version with coloured characters and extended ASCII graphics is quite
nice.

If you played a stoneage (i.e. pre-nethack) hack version, then you'll be
surprised by the changes it has undergone.



